"\n\n\n Naengmyeon\"\n  address=\"466, Hyoheng-ro, Byeongjeom-gu, Hwaseong-si, Gyeonggi-do\"\n  rating=4.5\n  tags=\"restaurant\"\n/>\n\n\n## Review\nCheonghakdong Chic Naengmyeon is a famous naengmyeon restaurant, so it is always crowded whenever you go.  \nStill, the parking lot is large and well-equipped, and the inside of the restaurant is quite spacious, so even if there is a wait, the turnover rate is high and you don't have to wait very long before being guided to a seat.  \n\nUpon entering the restaurant, you order at the counter first and make a prepayment.  \nOnce payment is done, the staff guides you to a seat.  \n\nThe seasoning (dadeqi) here is on the spicy side, so if you cannot eat spicy food well, it would be better to avoid bibim-naengmyeon.  \nAlternatively, you can ask for the seasoning to be less spicy when ordering.  \n\nWe ordered one regular mul-naengmyeon and one large mul-naengmyeon.  \nOrdering the large size didn't dramatically increase the portion, it was just slightly more noodles.  \nStill, if you are going to eat it anyway, I would recommend ordering the large size.  \n\nChic (arrowroot) water and warm broth are self-served.  \nIf you take a sip of the warm broth, you can immediately feel that the broth is quite rich, and even this single cup made me realize that this place is a true local favorite.  \n\nAfter drinking the broth and waiting for a short while, the ordered dishes came out faster than expected.  \nThe phrase \"high turnover rate\" was truly felt in moments like this.  \n\nAlthough you can add mustard and vinegar, I personally recommend eating it plain (as-is).  \nThat alone was rich enough in flavor, leaving absolutely no regrets.  \n\nAs rumored, it was indeed a great restaurant.\n## Pictures\n\n\n\n\n\n"